{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"Drafted the complete WI-961 intent spine set.\n\n| Row | Cell | Before | After | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SR-244 | row | new | “Transcript-derived usage records include coordinated nested agents” | Derived performance requirement under SN-026. |\n| LLR-347 | row | new | “Transcript usage is finalized once per message” | Counts final messages once and identifies open/partial cases. |\n| LLR-348 | row | new | “Transcript identity determines each invocation identity” | Pins deterministic invocation identity and role. |\n| LLR-349 | row | new | “Each recorded range is an ordered contribution” | Defines contribution key, cursor, and collision-free stamp. |\n| LLR-350 | row | new | “Existing contributions determine the next transcript range” | Defines exactly-once reads and fail-closed cursor handling. |\n| LLR-351 | row | new | “A service-recorded session is excluded from transcript duplication” | Applies D-002: service results omit sub-agents, so only main is skipped. |\n| LLR-352 | row | new | “The transcript reader refuses shapes outside its closed contract” | Closed-shape validation and per-transcript refusal. |\n| LLR-353 | row | new | “Ingest reads the ambient transcript home for one selected session” | Defines home/session selection and absence/refusal outcomes. |\n| LLR-354 | row | new | “Ingested logs carry contribution usage without transcript text” | Pins columns, values, and redaction. |\n| LLR-355 | row | new | “Usage ingest reports one defined command outcome per invocation” | Defines CLI stdout and exit outcomes. |\n| LLR-356 | row | new | “Close-out and headless completion ingest current and prior session tails” | Covers close-out and prior-handoff tail pickup. |\n| TC-386–TC-395 | rows | new | Ten arm-specific TCs | Cover identity, counting, finality, recovery, duplication avoidance, refusal, redaction, gate isolation, CLI, and guidance. |\n| IF-065 | requestors | `[\"scripts/agent_loop\", \"scripts/integrate\", \"scripts/session_service\"]` | adds `\"scripts/usage_ingest\"` | The command reads shared log metadata/worktree records. |\n| IF-065 | data | existing alphabet | adds `log_meta_text, worktree_records` | Names the seam functions used for exactly-once checks. |\n| IF-245 | requestors | existing requestors | adds `\"scripts/usage_ingest\"` | The command uses the Claude reader. |\n| IF-245 | data | existing adapter surface | adds `claude_session`, `transcript_usage`, `TranscriptRefused`, `TRANSCRIPT_TYPES` | Defines the reader-facing seam. |\n| IF-245 | notes | existing source note | adds ambient-home read/no-write statement | Records the transcript-read boundary. |\n| IF-246 | requestors | existing requestors | adds `\"scripts/usage_ingest\"` | The command records through the service seam. |\n| IF-305 | row | new | CLI seam owned by `scripts/usage_ingest` | Defines coordinator invocation, outcomes, and exits. |\n| id-watermark | IF/LLR/SR/TC marks | 304/346/243/385 | 305/356/244/395 | Allocated IDs once through `trace.py --bump-ids`. |\n\nAllocated IDs: SR-244; LLR-347–LLR-356; TC-386–TC-395; IF-305.\n\nBuilder targets named by the rows:\n\n- Symbols: `claude_session`, `transcript_usage`, `TranscriptRefused`, `TRANSCRIPT_TYPES`, `invocation_id`, `main`, `write_session_log`, plus completion guidance symbols.\n- Tests: the P2-table tests in `test_claude_transcripts.py`, `test_usage_ingest.py`, `test_usage_ingest_git.py`, and `test_prompts.py`, cited exactly by the corresponding TC rows.\n\nChecks run:\n\n- `check_trajectory.py --strict` completed with existing advisories plus the expected intent warning that IF-305 has no declared source contract yet.\n- `trace.py --strict` completed: `orphans=0 integrity=0`; it warned, as expected at intent, that IF-245 names not-yet-created `TRANSCRIPT_TYPES`.\n- Prescribed pytest command started successfully with the literal basetemp and emitted passing dots, but the tool response ended bef